{
  "_comment": [
    "Sample-data ARCHETYPES for the Disability Registry.",
    "",
    "These are not per-person fixtures. load_sample_data.py picks one archetype",
    "per registered person deterministically (hash of the person's id), so the",
    "sample set is reproducible, internally consistent, and independent of how",
    "many people the demography source happens to contain.",
    "",
    "Writing them as archetypes rather than rows is what keeps the person's",
    "denormalised unmet_support_needs_count honest: the loader derives it from",
    "the support rows it actually created, so the summary can never disagree",
    "with the detail the way a hand-written fixture set eventually does.",
    "",
    "`weight` sets how often an archetype is drawn. The distribution is loosely",
    "modelled on WHO World Report on Disability severity shares — most disability",
    "is mild-to-moderate, a small share is severe — so charts built on this data",
    "have a plausible shape rather than a uniform one.",
    "",
    "TEST_ is deliberately absent: these are demo records, not sanity fixtures.",
    "The sanity suite injects its own record (test/sanity/sanity/data_seed.py)."
  ],
